      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor(qa): share Matrix flows across channel drivers",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nQA Lab scenarios could select only one channel driver, which forced Matrix behavior to be duplicated when the same scenario needed both the live Matrix adapter and Crabline's Matrix provider bridge.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdd the small shared foundation needed for stacked Matrix QA migration work:\n\n- allow a QA Lab flow to declare multiple supported channel drivers while still requiring the selected channel to match;\n- map portable QA actor and conversation identifiers onto Crabline's Matrix endpoint without moving Matrix behavior into the QA adapter;\n- run the existing shared/per-room Matrix DM scenarios through either `--channel-driver crabline` or `--channel-driver live` using the normal QA Lab flow host;\n- keep coverage-report commands runnable by selecting a concrete supported driver.\n\nThis is stack PR 1 of 4. It does not migrate the legacy Matrix scenario/profile catalog, switch release workflows, or remove `qa-matrix`. Those changes remain in stacked successors so this foundation can be reviewed independently.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo shipped Matrix channel behavior changes. QA maintainers can execute the same two Matrix DM session scenarios against Crabline or the live Matrix adapter without adding a Matrix-specific scenario executor.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox through Crabbox: `tbx_01kx4kvpngzvbd4ck5846cj4qy` (`silver-barnacle`).\n  - Matrix Crabline transport tests: 2 passed, including outbound-only logical target restoration.\n  - Multi-driver suite-planning and coverage-command tests: 5 passed.\n  - QA Lab UI production build passed.\n- Identical Crabline/live DM flows passed before the split on the same nine-file behavior slice. Re-running the CLI after rebuilding on current `main` was blocked by delegated Testbox sync omitting tracked `extensions/qa-lab/src/mantis/cli.ts`; no changed file depends on Mantis.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- Fresh whole-branch Codex autoreview on `114bf82f34ea52da3f83551f8f58a1663a0505f4`: clean, no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Optional agent transcript omitted by orchestrator default because the user did not request inclusion.\n",
